## 3. Industry-Specific Risk
**Part A — Why This Company Can Compound:**  
ASML’s upstream trigger (customer CapEx spending) → Structural advantage (sole-source EUV lithography) → Downstream outcome (high-margin revenue and market share gains) → Feedback loop (reinvestment in R&D strengthens moat).  

**Durability verdict:** High — ASML’s technological leadership is self-reinforcing.  

**Part B — Capex Cycle Risk:**  
ASML is highly dependent on foundries (fab-lite model), exposed to semiconductor cycles. Its customer concentration in data center and consumer markets adds volatility risk.  

**Severity:** **HIGH** — dependency on cyclical CapEx spending with limited diversification.  

